  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Used 'gan {h}' (gan = hour/o'clock, numeral follows noun as elsewhere in Fon) and additive minutes with the comitative 'kpo ... kpo' and 'cɛju' (minute): 'gan wè kpo cɛju wǒ kpo' = 2:10. Minute numerals use Fon vigesimal forms (ko 20, gban 30, kanɖé 40, kanɖéwǒ 50, afɔtɔ́n 15, koatɔ́ɔ́n 25, gbanatɔ́ɔ́n 35, kanɖéatɔ́ɔ́n 45, kanɖéafɔtɔ́n 55); compound spelling and tone marks are best-effort. No half-hour word used (30 = 'cɛju gban') because I could not verify a Fon 'half' word for clock time. Also corrected hours[11] from 'ɖokpo-wǒ' to 'wěɖokpo' (Fon 11; 12 = wěwè, already correct). Needs a native-speaker check."
    }
  ]
